      "description": "Watch Plymouth vs Stockport County highlights and goals from League One on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 15, 2026. The atmosphere was electric at Home Park as Plymouth faced Stockport County on August 15, 2026, in a fixture that promised plenty of action. Both sides looked to establish their dominance early in the League One campaign, setting the stage for a compelling encounter. Clinical First Half from Stockport Stockport County started the match with intent, asserting their authority from the opening whistle. The breakthrough came in the 13th minute when Lewis Bate turned provider, delivering a pinpoint ball to Jack Diamond , who made no mistake in finding the back of the net. The early lead allowed the visitors to dictate the tempo, utilizing quick transitions to keep the Plymouth defense under constant pressure. The visitors’ dominance was further rewarded in the 26th minute. Kyle Wootton pounced on an opportunity to double the lead, clinical finishing ensuring Stockport County remained firmly in control. Plymouth struggled to find their rhythm, and although the game saw its share of physical challenges—highlighted by a yellow card for Jim McNulty in the 37th minute—the visitors headed into the tunnel at halftime with a significant two-goal cushion. Second Half Drama and Late Consolidation The restart brought little relief for the hosts, as Stockport County struck again shortly after the interval. In the 49th minute, Jack Diamond turned from scorer to creator, assisting Ryan Glover for the team’s third goal of the afternoon. Facing a daunting deficit, Plymouth turned to their bench, introducing Xavier Amaechi in the 57th minute to spark a revival. The tactical shift eventually bore fruit. In the 80th minute, Xavier Amaechi found the target to pull a goal back for the home side, giving the fans a glimmer of hope. However, Stockport managed the closing stages with composure. Despite late yellow cards for Julio Pleguezuelo and Aribim Pepple , and a flurry of substitutions including Lewis Fiorini and Brendan Sarpong-Wiredu , the visitors held firm to secure a convincing victory on the road."
